  "slug": "califur",
  "name": "Califur",
  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Califur (CF) was an annual furry convention in Southern California that succeeded ConFurence as the region's main furry event. It was organized by FENEC Adventures (\"Furries Enjoying the Natural Environments of California\"), a group founded by Robert \"Alohawolf\" Johnson, Dawn Britt and Dennis Carr for furry camping trips; after ConFurence ended in 2003, they were joined by ConFurence co-founders Mark Merlino and Rod O'Riley to plan a hotel-based convention. The first, Califur 0, was held in May 2004 in Irvine, and later editions took place in Costa Mesa, Irvine and Pomona, growing from 328 to over 1,400 attendees. Recurring events included a pet auction, cabaret, dances, gaming, a fursuit parade and the 18+ Califur After Dark. The final convention was held in May 2017.",
